 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the empire state\ncommercial production tax credit",
    "basePrintNo": "S8465",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8465-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§28, 210-B & 606, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8465\n\nSPONSOR: GOLDEN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending\nthe empire state commercial production tax credit\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would extend the Empire State Commercial Production tax cred-\nit, as enumerated in section 28 of the Tax Law, until the end of calen-\ndar year 2023. The credit is scheduled to sunset for taxable years\nbeginning before the end of 2018.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill extends the sunset for the qualified commercial\nproduction companies, currently scheduled in section 28 of the Tax Law\nfor taxable years beginning before the January 1, 2019, until taxable\nyears beginning on or after January 1, 2024.\n\nSection 2 and 3 make corresponding extensions to the provisions Covering\ncorporate franchise and personal income taxes.\n\nSection 4 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Empire State Commercial Production tax credit is an essential compo-\nnent of maintaining a viable and expanding commercial advertising busi-\nness in New York. Since the credit's enactment in 2006, commercial\nproduction activity in the State, after declining by more than 50\npercent the previous ten years, has increased 60 percent.\n\nUnfortunately, the credit is due to expire at the end of calendar year\n2018. This bill will extend the credit for 5 years, and align its effec-\ntive period to the State's film production credit to send a strong\nsignal of encouragement to firms considering doing commercials in New\nYork.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThe credit was last extended in Part J of Chapter 60 of the Laws of\n2016, and before than in 2014, 2012, and 2009.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nIncentives worth up to $7 million a year first to be paid during the\n2020 taxable year.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
